1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,459
A robot setting a table looks impressive. But a moved cup or a failed

2
00:00:05,459 --> 00:00:09,748
grasp can break that plan. Granted Robotics makes the recovery inspectable.

3
00:00:09,748 --> 00:00:14,037
Created by Shivam Gupta, it combines a clear operator workbench with

4
00:00:14,037 --> 00:00:15,207
reproducible simulation evidence.

5
00:00:15,207 --> 00:00:19,712
Here is the hosted workbench. Choose the physics backed cup and bowl

6
00:00:19,712 --> 00:00:24,217
task, then select grip loss. Validate the task in MuJoCo. The result

7
00:00:24,217 --> 00:00:27,596
shows measured placement errors and backend events. The illustration

8
00:00:27,596 --> 00:00:31,351
is clearly separate from that evidence. Replay the workflow, inspect

9
00:00:31,351 --> 00:00:36,232
the recovery, and export the JSON record. A guest can test the core

10
00:00:36,232 --> 00:00:38,860
flow, and Firebase sign in is available.

11
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:43,997
The React workbench accepts a task and shows the evidence. A FastAPI

12
00:00:43,997 --> 00:00:47,849
service validates requests, then runs the MuJoCo fixture. Optional

13
00:00:47,849 --> 00:00:52,130
camera and language validation can approve only the supported contract.

14
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:56,410
The controller and geometric monitor execute the task. Results include

15
00:00:56,410 --> 00:00:58,123
events and measured errors.

16
00:00:58,123 --> 00:01:02,463
A real camera image and instruction go to the constrained language

17
00:01:02,463 --> 00:01:06,409
validator. Separately, we trained a small joint target imitation policy

18
00:01:06,409 --> 00:01:10,354
on four hundred eighty inverse kinematics examples, with one hundred

19
00:01:10,354 --> 00:01:14,300
twenty held out. OpenVINO runs its proposals. Mandatory numerical correction

20
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:19,035
remains part of control. This is not an end to end VLA.

21
00:01:19,035 --> 00:01:23,573
This is actual MuJoCo rendering, separate from the browser illustration.

22
00:01:23,573 --> 00:01:28,565
Both SO101 arms move objects to predefined targets. An injected grip

23
00:01:28,565 --> 00:01:33,104
loss breaks the initial attempt. The controller detects the displaced

24
00:01:33,104 --> 00:01:37,642
object and follows a recovery path. Simplified grasp attachment and

25
00:01:37,642 --> 00:01:39,911
simulator state remain important limitations.

26
00:01:39,911 --> 00:01:44,987
We evaluated ten seeds in five conditions, for fifty runs. We varied

27
00:01:44,987 --> 00:01:48,793
object position, mass, friction, cylinder size, lighting, and table

28
00:01:48,793 --> 00:01:54,291
color. Grip loss completed ten out of ten with recovery, and zero without

29
00:01:54,291 --> 00:01:59,367
it. All ten obstacle cases blocked execution. A safe stop is reported

30
00:01:59,367 --> 00:02:01,059
separately from task completion.

31
00:02:01,059 --> 00:02:05,740
The per seed records make the result inspectable. Every grip loss recovery

32
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:10,032
trial completed, but errors still vary by initial condition. The comparison

33
00:02:10,032 --> 00:02:14,323
shows mean cup error falling from about one hundred sixty millimeters

34
00:02:14,323 --> 00:02:18,615
to about fifteen. This is a small controlled benchmark, not generalization

35
00:02:18,615 --> 00:02:19,785
to new tasks.

36
00:02:19,785 --> 00:02:24,491
OpenVINO runs both the geometric graph and the learned joint target

37
00:02:24,491 --> 00:02:28,769
policy. In ten recovery trials, learned proposals plus correction reduced

38
00:02:28,769 --> 00:02:33,048
average numerical iterations by five point three percent. Both approaches

39
00:02:33,048 --> 00:02:37,326
completed every trial. The learned policy median inference was thirty

40
00:02:37,326 --> 00:02:41,177
seven microseconds on Apple hardware. Intel validation remains open.

41
00:02:41,177 --> 00:02:45,893
Twenty nine backend tests pass, covering task rejection, provider failures,

42
00:02:45,893 --> 00:02:50,137
safety checks, and learned policy reference accuracy. The repository

43
00:02:50,137 --> 00:02:53,910
includes reproducible training, evaluation, and device benchmark commands.

44
00:02:53,910 --> 00:03:00,041
The biggest remaining gaps against the brief are an end to end VLA,

45
00:03:00,041 --> 00:03:04,758
richer complementary manipulation, and a final Intel Core Ultra demonstration.

46
00:03:04,758 --> 00:03:09,396
The business starts with a small paid pilot, not a market size claim.

47
00:03:09,396 --> 00:03:13,321
We would import one integrator task and its recurring failure cases.

48
00:03:13,321 --> 00:03:17,603
We would measure diagnosis time before and after. A five hundred dollar

49
00:03:17,603 --> 00:03:21,884
monthly workspace is a pricing test. At an assumed seventy five dollars

50
00:03:21,884 --> 00:03:25,096
an engineer hour, seven saved hours covers that fee.

51
00:03:25,096 --> 00:03:30,054
The next milestone is a policy that reasons directly over vision and

52
00:03:30,054 --> 00:03:34,599
language. We also need a richer dual arm task, broader randomization,

53
00:03:34,599 --> 00:03:39,558
and an Intel Core Ultra run. Before commercial use, the product needs

54
00:03:39,558 --> 00:03:42,863
durable tenant storage, workload controls, and operational monitoring.

55
00:03:42,863 --> 00:03:45,755
Hardware safety validation is a separate effort.

56
00:03:45,755 --> 00:03:50,085
Granted Robotics makes the recovery part of the product. Review the

57
00:03:50,085 --> 00:03:54,415
workbench, replay the actual physics, and inspect the per seed records.

58
00:03:54,415 --> 00:03:59,139
The repository and demo are public. Created by Shivam Gupta for the

59
00:03:59,139 --> 00:04:00,714
AI Infra Summit Hackathon.
